{"id":409,"name":"rampardos","speciesId":409,"dex":409,"form":"normal","generation":4,"types":["rock"],"stats":{"hp":97,"attack":165,"defense":60,"special-attack":65,"special-defense":50,"speed":58},"abilities":[{"name":"mold-breaker","hidden":false},{"name":"sheer-force","hidden":true}],"height":16,"weight":1025,"baseExp":173,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/409.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/409.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/409.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/409.ogg","genus":"Head Butt Pokémon","genusPt":"Cabeçada Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"diamond","text":"Its powerful head butt has enough power to shatter even the most durable things upon impact."},{"version":"pearl","text":"Its skull is as hard as iron. It is a brute that tears down jungle trees while catching prey."},{"version":"platinum","text":"If two were to smash their heads together, their foot-thick skulls would keep them from fainting."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"Its skull withstands impacts of any magnitude. As a result, its brain never gets the chance to grow."},{"version":"sun","text":"The result of repeated headbutts is a skull grown thick and hard. However, its brain has shrunk in size compared with Cranidos’s."},{"version":"moon","text":"Records exist of a revived fossil that evolved into Rampardos. It proceeded to escape and then destroy a skyscraper with a headbutt."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"In ancient times, people would dig up fossils of this Pokémon and use its skull, which is harder than steel, to make helmets."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"This ancient Pokémon used headbutts skillfully. Its brain was really small, so some theories suggest that its stupidity led to its extinction."},{"version":"